Privacy Policy — Debt Notes 2.1

Debt Notes 2.1 is designed to help users manage their debt and expense records while respecting their privacy.

1. Information Collection

Debt Notes 2.1 does not collect or send your personal information to the developer, administrator, or any external server.

The information you enter into the application, such as debt records, expense details, notes, images, or signatures, is used only for the application's functionality on your device.

2. Data Storage

Your records are stored locally on your device according to the application's storage implementation.

The developer does not receive or have access to your records through the application.

3. Data Sharing

We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with the developer, administrator, advertisers, or other third parties.

4. Internet Access

The core debt and expense management features are designed to work offline. Your records are not uploaded to a developer-controlled server.

5. Images and Signatures

If you choose to add images or signatures, they are used only for the records you create in the application. They are not intentionally transmitted to the developer or administrator.

6. Notifications

If notification permission is enabled, the application may use your device's notification system to provide reminders or other app-related notifications.

7. Your Responsibility

Because your records are stored on your device, you are responsible for keeping your device secure and maintaining your own backups if needed.

8. Changes to This Privacy Policy

If the application's data practices change in the future, this Privacy Policy will be updated accordingly.

9. Contact

For questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please contact the developer through the contact information provided in the application's About section or GitHub repository.

---

In simple terms:
Debt Notes 2.1 does not collect your personal information and send it to the developer/admin. Your debt and expense records remain on your device and are used by the application for its intended features.
